language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Langford pairing: arrange two copies of each number 1..k in one sequence of 2k positions so that the two copies of v have v numbers between them.
given k : int(1..)
find sol : matrix indexed by [int(1..2*k)] of int(1..k)
find pos : matrix indexed by [int(1..k), int(1..2)] of int(1..2*k)

branching on [pos]

such that
$ the two copies of v have v numbers between them: the second copy is v + 1 positions after the first
forAll v : int(1..k) . (pos[v,2] = pos[v,1] + v + 1),
$ every position of the sequence is taken by exactly one copy of a number
allDiff(flatten(pos)),
$ the sequence holds the number v at both copies of v
forAll v : int(1..k) . forAll j : int(1..2) . (sol[pos[v,j]] = v)
